# CCPC NEW dedicated production HTTPS gateway - REVIEW TEMPLATE ONLY.
# Do not install/start/reload Caddy or open firewall ports by committing this file.
# Caddy runs on the NEW Ubuntu host, not as a Docker-published 443 container.
# Approved operator-selected LAN hostname: ccpcerp.internal
# Requires explicit operator-provided values:
#   CCPC_TLS_FULLCHAIN_FILE    approved readable full-chain PEM certificate
#   CCPC_TLS_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE  approved protected PEM private key
# Required internal DNS A record: ccpcerp.internal -> 192.168.50.186.
# Certificate SAN MUST contain DNS:ccpcerp.internal; deploy issuer root trust
# to approved Windows clients; protect and back up CA signing keys off-host.
# Configure certificate chain, private key permissions, DNS and client trust
# outside GitHub. Never supply credential contents in commits or chat.
# Host-only upstream is now available from a separately guarded systemd
# socket relay at 127.0.0.1:8080, forwarding to NEW A3 private Docker frontend.
# Operator-reported on 2026-11-11: socket active, bound ONLY to localhost,
# GET /login returned HTTP 200 with Frappe internal Host ccpcerp.local.
# The A3 frontend itself has NO Docker host-published ports and must not be
# recreated or published just to run this gateway.
# This still requires a trusted SAN-matching certificate, on-host Caddyfile
# adapter/runtime validation, LAN-scoped firewall and true external denial.
{
    admin off
    auto_https off
    servers 192.168.50.186:443 {
        protocols h1 h2
        strict_sni_host on
    }
}

https://ccpcerp.internal:443 {
    bind 192.168.50.186
    tls {$CCPC_TLS_FULLCHAIN_FILE} {$CCPC_TLS_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE}
    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
}
